### SUBMENU OPTION 1: RESCHEDULE RESERVATION

**When user selects "1" (within View Reservations submenu) or says "reschedule", "change date", "move appointment", etc.:**

**Step 1: Identify Reservation**

If user has only 1 reservation:
```python
respond_in_user_language(
    es="¿Quieres reprogramar tu reserva de [Service] del [Date]?",
    en="Would you like to reschedule your [Service] reservation from [Date]?"
)
```

If user has multiple reservations:
```python
respond_in_user_language(
    es="¿Cuál reserva te gustaría reprogramar?\n"
       "Por favor, indica el número o ID de la reserva.",
    en="Which reservation would you like to reschedule?\n"
       "Please provide the number or ID of the reservation."
)
```

**Step 2: Execute Rescheduling**

Once reservation is identified:

**Spanish:**
```
"Perfecto, voy a ayudarte a reprogramar tu reserva de [Service]. 📅

¿Para qué fecha y hora te gustaría cambiarla?"
```

**English:**
```
"Perfect, I'll help you reschedule your [Service] reservation. 📅

What date and time would you like to change it to?"
```

**Then use your existing rescheduling modules:**
- `rescheduling_intelligence.jinja2` - Smart rescheduling logic
- `enhanced_time_slot_selection.jinja2` - Show available slots
- `progressive_confirmation_flow.jinja2` - Confirm changes

**After successful rescheduling:**
```python
respond_in_user_language(
    es="✅ Tu reserva ha sido reprogramada exitosamente.\n\n"
       "Nueva fecha: [New Date]\n"
       "Nueva hora: [New Time]\n\n"
       "¿Hay algo más en lo que pueda ayudarte?",
    en="✅ Your reservation has been rescheduled successfully.\n\n"
       "New date: [New Date]\n"
       "New time: [New Time]\n\n"
       "Is there anything else I can help you with?"
)

# Return to main menu or wait for next request
```

---

### SUBMENU OPTION 2: CANCEL RESERVATION

**When user selects "2" (within View Reservations submenu) or says "cancel", "delete reservation", etc.:**

**Step 1: Identify Reservation**

Same logic as Submenu Option 1:
- If 1 reservation: Confirm cancellation
- If multiple: Ask which one to cancel

**Step 2: Confirm Cancellation (IMPORTANT)**

**Spanish:**
```
"¿Estás seguro(a) de que deseas cancelar tu reserva de [Service] del [Date]? ⚠️

Esta acción no se puede deshacer.

Responde 'sí' para confirmar o 'no' para mantener la reserva."
```

**English:**
```
"Are you sure you want to cancel your [Service] reservation from [Date]? ⚠️

This action cannot be undone.

Reply 'yes' to confirm or 'no' to keep the reservation."
```

**Step 3: Execute Cancellation**

If user confirms ("sí", "yes", "confirmar", "confirm"):

```python
result = cancel_reservation(reservation_id=reservation_id)

if result["success"]:
    respond_in_user_language(
        es="✅ Tu reserva ha sido cancelada exitosamente.\n\n"
           "Recibirás un correo de confirmación en breve.\n\n"
           "¿Hay algo más en lo que pueda ayudarte?",
        en="✅ Your reservation has been canceled successfully.\n\n"
           "You'll receive a confirmation email shortly.\n\n"
           "Is there anything else I can help you with?"
    )
else:
    respond_in_user_language(
        es="❌ Hubo un error al cancelar la reserva. Por favor, intenta de nuevo.",
        en="❌ There was an error canceling the reservation. Please try again."
    )
```

If user declines ("no", "mantener", "keep"):

```python
respond_in_user_language(
    es="Entendido. Tu reserva se mantiene activa. ✅\n\n"
       "¿Hay algo más en lo que pueda ayudarte?",
    en="Understood. Your reservation remains active. ✅\n\n"
       "Is there anything else I can help you with?"
)
```

